# Every file is checked out exactly as it is stored, with no line ending conversion.
#
# Git for Windows turns on core.autocrlf by default, which rewrites every text file on
# checkout. Editors that compare a file's bytes against the last commit, HyCreator among
# them, then report every text file in the mod as changed, and one commit sends them all.
# Turning conversion off removes that, whatever the computer's own git settings are.
* -text

# These are text, and every one of them is stored with LF endings. Marking them as text
# keeps it that way when a program on Windows saves one with CRLF endings: the commit stores
# LF and checkout writes LF, so the file on disk always matches what is stored.
#
# Everything not named here stays untouched, so a picture, a sound or a binary file can
# never be altered by a line ending rule that guessed wrong.
*.json            text eol=lf
*.patch           text eol=lf
*.lang            text eol=lf
*.ui              text eol=lf
*.blockymodel     text eol=lf
*.blockyanim      text eol=lf
*.bbmodel         text eol=lf
*.particlesystem  text eol=lf
*.particlespawner text eol=lf
*.java            text eol=lf
*.gradle          text eol=lf
*.properties      text eol=lf
*.xml             text eol=lf
*.md              text eol=lf
*.gitignore       text eol=lf
*.gitattributes   text eol=lf
